@startuml AS03-federated-sso-via-as
!include ../includes/C4_Sequence_Macros.puml

title AS03 — Federated enterprise SSO through the internal AS\n(upstream IdP → AS maps identity → AS mints tokens; no upstream token at API)

C4Seq_User()
C4Seq_WebUI()
C4Seq_AuthServer()
C4Seq_CredStore()
C4Seq_KeyProvider()
C4Seq_IdP()
C4Seq_API()
C4Seq_Audit()
C4Seq_OTEL()

== Browser initiates sign-in at the AS ==

seqUser -> seqWebUI : Sign in (A01)
seqWebUI -> seqAuthServer : GET /authorize (response_type=code, PKCE S256,\nresource=API or UI audience)
ControlNote(seqAuthServer, "IA-2, IA-8", "V-222400, V-222401, V-222522", "AS is the single issuer; IdP is federated upstream (ARCH-AUTH-FEDERATION / CAP-SSO)")

seqAuthServer -> seqIdP : redirect / OIDC authorize (or SAML)
seqIdP --> seqUser : IdP login UI
seqUser -> seqIdP : credentials / MFA at enterprise IdP
seqIdP --> seqAuthServer : id_token / assertion (code + tokens to AS only)
ControlNote(seqAuthServer, "IA-5, SC-23", "V-222403, V-222404", "AS validates assertion (iss, aud=AS client, signature, nonce); IdP tokens never reach ReqAML API")

seqAuthServer -> seqCredStore : map external_sub → identity (e.g. oidc:dan-raby → dan)\nload grants server-side
AuthAuditLog("auth:federated:signin allow")
seqAuthServer -> seqKeyProvider : sign(access token, kid) — Transit
seqAuthServer --> seqWebUI : code → tokens (iss=ReqAML AS, aud=API/UI)\n+ rotating refresh
ControlNote(seqAuthServer, "SC-12(3), IA-5(6)", "V-222570", "Tokens minted by AS; signing keys in OpenBao (KS02)")

== API accepts only internal-AS tokens ==

seqWebUI -> seqAPI : AuthenticatedCall (Bearer AS token)
TokenValidate(seqAPI, "https://reqaml/api")
ControlNote(seqAPI, "IA-2, AC-3", "TBD (ASD V6R4)", "Upstream IdP token presented at API → 401 (FIX-DENY-UPSTREAM-TOKEN-AT-API)")
seqAPI --> seqWebUI : 200 + Scoped View context

@enduml
